    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nhipatterns\n\n### Description\n\nThe new anticonceal feature in neovim 0.10 opens up the possibility of displaying inlay virtual text with the hipatterns extmarks instead of (or in addition to) just highlights. That way, we could for example display a dot of the corresponding color next to a hex code rather than coloring the code itself (which can sometimes conflict with other highlights).\r\n\r\nI don't believe this should be the default but it doesn't sound too out of scope for this plugin to offer this as an option, since it already defines extmarks anyway.\r\n\r\nI don't know if it would be best to hold off until 0.10 is released? I don't think that part of the API will change.",
